er-left window across scene, bright gold patch on counter/floor. Steam from kettle/mug. Dust motes.\n\nNeed maybe cat on window sill or floor patchof sun. A ginger cat curled on a small rug in front? That adds coziness. But complexity. Maybe a striped tabby cat sitting on counter next to bowl, silhouette. Or sleeping cat on window sill. Sill at y~580, x 420..880. Cat lying on right side of window sill (x 720..860), orange with darker stripes, tail curled. Might block view slightly but cute. Sink below.\n\nCould also do a hanging pendant light? Morning doesn't need. Hanging herbs in front of window at top. Copper pots hanging left of window.\n\nColor palette: warm cream, honey oak, sage green, terracotta, copper, soft blue sky, golden light, off-white ceramics. Maybe accent dusty rose.\n\nNeed realistic shapes via gradients and layering.\n\nImplementation approach:\n- Utility functions: lerp color, vertical_gradient, rounded_rect, polygon, ellipse w/ shading, texture.\n- Draw at scale 2 (3200x2400) with coordinates in base units scaled by S. Make helper transform functions.\n- Use draw rounded_rectangle, polygon, ellipse. For gradients inside shapes: create gradient image mask via shape on separate mask. For complex shapes, use rounded mask and composite.\n- Add shadows beneath objects with translucent ellipses/rounded rectangles.\n- Outlines with darker colors at low width to give illustration feel (but not cartoonish).\n- Draw within layers.\n\nNeed possible use custom RGBA colors. PIL supports. Need gradients with alpha. Construct e.g. gradient_rect(size, top, bottom). Mask shapes.\n\nMaybe easiest create at base size 1600x1200 using anti-alias 2x. All draw coords multiply by scale. Create gradient at 2x itself maybe costly but okay. 3200x2400 memory ~30MB each. Fine.\n\nLet's set S=2, W=1600,H=1200.\n\nLayer order:\n1. Background wall.\n  - gradient from light warm top #f8ead4 to slightly darker #ead5b5 bottom.\n  - subtle plaster texture patches and noise.\n  - maybe vertical paneling? Wainscoting below counter hidden; still visible sides.\n2. Window and outside view.\n  - shadow around frame; frame wood.\n  - exterior sky gradient, sun disc glow, distant hills, trees.\n  - panes with mullions, reflection diagonal highlights.\n  - sill.\n3. Shelves & wall decor:\n  - Left open shelf with jars/plants/books, hanging copper pans maybe.\n  - Right upper shelf with crocks and plant.\n  - Herb bundle hanging near window.\n4. Counter + lower cabinets:\n  - counter slab with edge, cabinets sage, panels, brass knobs.\n  - sink basin + faucet.\n5. Objects on counter:\n  - Left of sink: cutting board with bread, bowl of lemons, jar.\n  - Right: kettle on low flame? Maybe stovetop not counter. Better range built into right.\nLet's design exact.\n\nMaybe room:\n- Back wall width all.\n- Counter across from x=0 to 1600, y=820 top. Sink centered under window.\n- Lower cabinets y=850..1060. Floor y=1060..1200.\n- Range on right x=1190..1500: stainless/cream oven front with 4 burners, kettle on top. Then counter from sink to range. If range top also at 825. Make freestanding range with oven front down to floor (y=1075), and no lower cabinet there.\n- Left side x=120..430: counter with cutting board etc, below cabinets.\n- Far left tall cabinet maybe x=0..110. Fine.\n\nUpper:\n- Left wall shelf x=75..340 y=380, 520, 640? 2 floating wood shelves with crockery.\n- Window x=400..900 y=100..600.\n- Right upper open shelf x=1060..1515 y=390 with plates/canisters.\n- Copper pan hanging at x=930..1050 maybe between window and shelves.\n\nCounter items:\n- sink x=470..820, white farmhouse. Faucet at x=640, brass gooseneck.\n- Left board x=160..380 leaning? cutting board flat with toast and bread. Bowl of lemons x=100..200? Need space.\n- Right of sink x=900..1140: mug and small plant, bread box maybe.\n- Range x=1210..1490 with kettle, teapot, small pot.\n- On window sill: potted herbs (basil), little jar, cat? Sill depth only perhaps 756? Hmm window bottom 600, sill y=580..625. Cat maybe too large. Could put cat on floor sun patch front-right or on counter. A sleeping cat curled on counter near right adds charm but more shape.\nMaybe cat on a stool at left? Let's make a ginger cat sitting on counter far left at x=230..360 y=700..840, back to viewer, silhouetted by light. But would be near shelf/counter. Cute. Yet cat and bread may crowd.\n\nAlternative: small cat sleeping on windowsill curled into a ball, at right window x=740..865. Sill depth can support. That is iconic cozy. Body oval orange with stripes, ears, tail, closed eyes. Size 130x60. It can sit in front of lower right pane? Sure. Then herbs on left sill.\n\nNeed \"morning\": sun outside upper leftish; rays enter window at diagonal from x=520,y=140 toward x=1080,y=820. Use translucent warm polygons overlay. Also bright patch on counter and floor. Dust motes as small glowing dots.\n\nNeed perhaps subtle perspective lines. Straight-on composition is okay but can feel flat. Add perspective: window sill and counters with slight perspective, floor tiles converging. But straight-on can still good with depth from shadows. Use counters horizontal and floor tiles horizontal rows. Maybe slight vanishing point at center, but complex. Could rely on atmospheric shading.\n\nNeed style: rich illustration with painterly brush texture. We can overlay noise, soft light bloom, vignette.\n\nNeed maybe create a title? User just asks draw, no text needed. Avoid text.\n\nLet's implement with many helper functions:\n\n- PIL Image, ImageDraw, ImageFilter, ImageChops.\n- scale coords: helper `P(x,y)` maybe draw uses scaled direct. Better define `s(x)` and use `scale_rect`. But with many calls tedious. Could draw at base 1600x1200 directly, then upscale 2.5x? Drawing at 1600 then upscaling would blur. Better draw at 3200x2400 using transform wrapper functions that accept base coords. Implement custom class `Canvas` with methods:\n  - polygon(points, fill, outline=None, width=0)\n  - rounded_rect(box, radius, fill, outline=None, width=0)\n  - ellipse(box,...)\n  - line(points, fill, width)\n  - arc\n  - gradient_shape(mask_draw_fn, c1,c2, direction='v', box) etc.\n  - shadow maybe.\n\nActually easiest set SS=2 and wrapper `sc(v)=round(v*SS)`. For box: [x0*S, y0*S, ...]. Radius similarly. Width too. Every drawi","truncated":true}
{"type":"tool_call","callId":"call_00_0Kj9FB1htf1RKqFTR54H5179","tool":"bash","input":{"command":"mkdir -p /tmp/vellery-la2gxpdr/work && cat > /tmp/vellery-la2gxpdr/work/draw_kitchen.py <<'PY'\nfrom PIL import Image, ImageDraw, ImageFilter, ImageChops\nimport math, random\n\nW, H = 1600, 1200\nS = 2\nrandom.seed(42)\n\nimg = Image.new(\"RGB\", (W*S, H*S), \"#f2e2cb\")\nd = ImageDraw.Draw(img, \"RGBA\")\n\ndef X(v):\n    return int(round(v*S))\n\ndef B(b):\n    return tuple(X(v) for v in b)\n\ndef P(ps):\n    return [(X(x), X(y)) for x,y in ps]\n\ndef col(c):\n    if isinstance(c, str):\n        from PIL import ImageColor\n        return ImageColor.getrgb(c)\n    return tuple(c[:3])\n\ndef fill_alpha(c):\n    if len(c)==4: return c\n    return (*col(c), 255)\n\ndef line(ps, fill, width=1, joint=\"curve\"):\n    d.line(P(ps), fill=fill_alpha(fill), width=max(1, X(width)), joint=joint)\n\ndef poly(ps, fill, outline=None, width=1):\n    d.polygon(P(ps), fill=fill_alpha(fill))\n    if outline:\n        d.line(P(ps)+[P(ps)[0]], fill=fill_alpha(outline), width=max(1,X(width)), joint=\"curve\")\n\ndef ellipse(b, fill, outline=None, width=1):\n    d.ellipse(B(b), fill=fill_alpha(fill))\n    if outline:\n        d.ellipse(B(b), outline=fill_alpha(outline), width=max(1,X(width)))\n\ndef rrect(b, r, fill, outline=None, width=1):\n    d.rounded_rectangle(B(b), radius=X(r), fill=fill_alpha(fill))\n    if outline:\n        d.rounded_rectangle(B(b), radius=X(r), outline=fill_alpha(outline), width=max(1,X(width)))\n\ndef rectangle(b, fill, outline=None, width=1):\n    d.rectangle(B(b), fill=fill_alpha(fill))\n    if outline:\n        d.rectangle(B(b), outline=fill_alpha(outline), width=max(1,X(width)))\n\ndef lin_gradient(w, h, c0, c1, horizontal=False):\n    c0 = col(c0); c1 = col(c1)\n    if horizontal:\n        im = Image.new(\"RGB\", (w,1))\n    else:\n        im = Image.new(\"RGB\", (1,h))\n    px = im.load()\n    n = w if horizontal else h\n    for i in range(n):\n        t = i/max(1,n-1)\n        c = tuple(round(c0[k]*(1-t)+c1[k]*t) for k in range(3))\n        if horizontal: px[i,0] = c\n        else: px[0,i] = c\n    return im.resize((w,h), Image.BILINEAR)\n\ndef grad_rect(b, c0, c1, radius=0, horizontal=False, outline=None, width=1):\n    x0,y0,x1,y1 = [X(v) for v in b]\n    bw,bh = max(1,x1-x0), max(1,y1-y0)\n    g = lin_gradient(bw,bh,c0,c1,horizontal)\n    mask = Image.new(\"L\",(bw,bh),0)\n    md = ImageDraw.Draw(mask)\n    if radius>0:\n        md.rounded_rectangle((0,0,bw-1,bh-1), radius=X(radius), fill=255)\n    else:\n        md.rectangle((0,0,bw-1,bh-1), fill=255)\n    img.paste(g,(x0,y0),mask)\n    if outline:\n        rrect(b,radius,outline,None,0)\n        d.rounded_rectangle(B(b), radius=X(radius), outline=fill_alpha(outline), width=max(1,X(width)))\n\ndef radial_glow(cx, cy, rx, ry, color, alpha=120, blur=18, screen=False):\n    x0,y0 = X(cx-rx), X(cy-ry)\n    x1,y1 = X(cx+rx), X(cy+ry)\n    w,h = max(1,x1-x0), max(1,y1-y0)\n    layer = Image.new(\"RGBA\",(w,h),(0,0,0,0))\n    ld = ImageDraw.Draw(layer)\n    ld.ellipse((0,0,w-1,h-1), fill=(*col(color), alpha))\n    layer = layer.filter(ImageFilter.GaussianBlur(X(blur)))\n    base = img.convert(\"RGBA\")\n    tmp = Image.new(\"RGBA\", base.size, (0,0,0,0))\n    tmp.alpha_composite(layer,(x0,y0))\n    if screen:\n        base = Image.alpha_composite(base,tmp)\n    else:\n        base = Image.alpha_composite(base,tmp)\n    img.paste(base.convert(\"RGB\"))\n    d._image = img\n\ndef soft_shadow(b, offset=(0,8), blur=10, color=(70,40,20), alpha=80, radius=0):\n    x0,y0,x1,y1 = [X(v) for v in b]\n    ox,oy = X(offset[0]), X(offset[1])\n    pad = X(blur)*2 + 4\n    lw,lh = (x1-x0)+2*pad, (y1-y0)+2*pad\n    mask = Image.new(\"L\",(lw,lh),0)\n    md = ImageDraw.Draw(mask)\n    if radius>0:\n        md.rounded_rectangle((pad+ox,pad+oy,pad+x1-x0+ox,pad+y1-y0+oy), radius=X(radius), fill=alpha)\n    else:\n        md.rectangle((pad+ox,pad+oy,pad+x1-x0+ox,pad+y1-y0+oy), fill=alpha)\n    mask = mask.filter(ImageFilter.GaussianBlur(X(blur)))\n    img.paste(col(color),(x0-pad,y0-pad),mask)\n    d._image = img\n\ndef soft_ellipse_shadow(b, blur=12, color=(60,35,20), alpha=70):\n    x0,y0,x1,y1 = [X(v) for v in b]\n    pad = X(blur)*2+4\n    w,h = x1-x0+2*pad, y1-y0+2*pad\n    mask = Image.new(\"L\",(w,h),0)\n    ImageDraw.Draw(mask).ellipse((pad,pad,pad+x1-x0,pad+y1-y0), fill=alpha)\n    mask = mask.filter(ImageFilter.GaussianBlur(X(blur)))\n    img.paste(col(color),(x0-pad,y0-pad),mask)\n    d._image = img\n\ndef radial_rect_glow(b, color, alpha=80, blur=20):\n    # soft light inside a rectangular region\n    x0,y0,x1,y1 = [X(v) for v in b]\n    pad = X(blur)*2\n    w,h = x1-x0+2*pad, y1-y0+2*pad\n    mask = Image.new(\"L\",(w,h),0)\n    ImageDraw.Draw(mask).rounded_rectangle((pad,pad,pad+x1-x0,pad+y1-y0),radius=X(20),fill=alpha)\n    mask = mask.filter(ImageFilter.GaussianBlur(X(blur)))\n    img.paste(col(color),(x0-pad,y0-pad),mask)\n    d._image = img\n\n# soft brush helper for highlights\ndef brush_line(ps, fill, width=6, blur=3):\n    layer = Image.new(\"RGBA\", img.size, (0,0,0,0))\n    ld = ImageDraw.Draw(layer)\n    ld.line(P(ps), fill=fill_alpha(fill), width=max(1,X(width)), joint=\"curve\")\n    for p in (ps[0], ps[-1]):\n        ld.ellipse((X(p[0]-width/2),X(p[1]-width/2),X(p[0]+width/2),X(p[1]+width/2)), fill=fill_alpha(fill))\n    layer = layer.filter(ImageFilter.GaussianBlur(X(blur)))\n    img.paste(Image.alpha_composite(img.convert(\"RGBA\"),layer).convert(\"RGB\"))\n    d._image = img\n\n# ---------- WALL ----------\nwall_grad = lin_gradient(W*S, H*S, \"#faefdd\", \"#e8ceb0\")\nimg.paste(wall_grad,(0,0))\n# broad uneven plaster passages\nfor i in range(35):\n    x = random.uniform(-100, W)\n    y = random.uniform(-50, 760)\n    rx = random.uniform(80, 320); ry = random.uniform(40, 160)\n    c = random.choice([\"#fff6e7\", \"#f0d9ba\", \"#efd7ba\"])\n    a = random.randint(8, 22)\n    radial_glow(x,y,rx,ry,c,a,60)\n\n# pale blue-grey undertone in shadows\nfor (x,y,rx,ry,a) in [(90,760,220,190,22),(1490,720,260,220,28),(250,120,300,160,12)]:\n    radial_glow(x,y,rx,ry,\"#b9b3a0\",a,80)\n\n# wainscot beadboard strips (small, visible at edges)\nfor x in range(20, 1580, 26):\n    line([(x,1088),(x,1092)],\"#d8c0a2\",1)\n\n# ---------- WINDOW (outside view first) ----------\n# wall shadow behind frame\nsoft_shadow((398,86,902,642), offset=(18,22), blur=26, color=(94,62,35), alpha=80, radius=14)\n# outer frame\ngrad_rect((394,82,906,636), \"#d5a064\", \"#8d5632\", radius=14, horizontal=False,\n          outline=\"#744424\", width=2)\n# frame top highlight\nrrect((404,90,896,106), 7, \"#e4b77f\")\n# inner bevel shadow\nrrect((414,102,886,620), 9, \"#6e4327\")\n# glass opening\nOX0,OY0,OX1,OY1 = 430,118,870,604\ngrad_rect((OX0,OY0,OX1,OY1), \"#a9c4cc\", \"#f4d3a0\", radius=2)\n\n# outside sky\nsky = lin_gradient(X(OX1-OX0), X(OY1-OY0), \"#86abc1\", \"#f8d6a0\")\n# deepen sky top\ntop_ov = Image.new(\"RGBA\", sky.size,(0,0,0,0))\ntd = ImageDraw.Draw(top_ov)\nfor i in range(sky.size[1]):\n    pass\nimg.paste(sky,(X(OX0),X(OY0)))\n# clouds\nfor (cx,cy,rx,ry,a) in [(510,210,60,17,40),(575,178,42,13,28),(760,240,74,19,30),(830,195,50,13,26)]:\n    radial_glow(cx,cy,rx,ry,\"#f9f4df\",a,10)\n# sun glow and disc\nradial_glow(702,408,190,190,\"#ffe6a8\",95,55)\nradial_glow(702,408,92,92,\"#fff0bf\",130,24)\nellipse((678,384,726,432),\"#fff6d8\")\n# hills\npoly([(430,462),(500,435),(566,452),(620,428),(690,450),(758,430),(820,450),(870,438),(870,510),(430,510)], \"#9aa59a\")\npoly([(430,492),(495,465),(566,484),(620,466),(695,488),(760,468),(820,488),(870,478),(870,560),(430,560)], \"#8c997d\")\npoly([(430,530),(490,506),(560,520),(620,502),(680,526),(750,510),(810,528),(870,513),(870,604),(430,604)], \"#67805d\")\n# distant warm field\npoly([(430,532),(520,520),(610,534),(700,519),(790,534),(870,524),(870,580),(430,580)], \"#84925f\")\n# morning haze\nradial_glow(680,500,220,100,\"#f6d69b\",40,30)\n# trees / bushes outside\n# left tree\nline([(482,510),(482,580)],\"#4e4933\",5)\nfor (cx,cy,rx,ry,c) in [(468,475,30,32,\"#506c49\"),(500,470,35,38,\"#5f7b50\"),(475,500,42,24,\"#496340\"),(515,500,32,20,\"#5d7a4d\")]:\n    ellipse((cx-rx,cy-ry,cx+rx,cy+ry),c)\n# sunlit leaves\nfor (cx,cy,rx,ry) in [(470,458,10,6),(504,464,12,7),(486,486,10,5),(514,490,8,5)]:\n    ellipse((cx-rx,cy-ry,cx+rx,cy+ry),\"#a9b774\")\n# right bushes\nfor (cx,cy,rx,ry,c) in [(795,530,34,24,\"#7b8552\"),(830,522,28,20,\"#899461\"),(858,538,25,18,\"#6d7b4c\")]:\n    ellipse((cx-rx,cy-ry,cx+rx,cy+ry),c)\n# tiny fence in distance\nfor x in range(","description":"Write first half of kitchen illustration script"},"truncated":true}
